module

public import StacksFrontier.AlgebraicGeometry.Divisors.EffectiveCartier.UFDExtension
public import StacksFrontier.AlgebraicGeometry.Divisors.EffectiveCartierStalk.StalkwiseRegular
public import StacksFrontier.AlgebraicGeometry.Morphisms.EtaleBasics.NormalCrossings.StalkIdeal
public import StacksFrontier.RingTheory.Henselian.HenselizationMinimalPrimes
public import StacksFrontier.RingTheory.Henselian.PrincipalIdealDescent
public import StacksFrontier.RingTheory.RegularLocalRing.StrictHenselizationParameters

/-!
# Local equations recovered from the strict henselizations

Let `X` be a locally Noetherian scheme and `D` a closed subscheme, given by its ideal sheaf data.
Say that `D` *has strict normal crossings at the strict henselizations* when, for every point `p`
of `D`, the inverse image of `D` under the canonical morphism
`Spec 𝒪^{sh}_{X, p} ⟶ Spec 𝒪_{X, p} ⟶ X` is a strict normal crossings divisor. This is condition
(2) of Tag 0CBS, and this file descends from it everything about `D` that can be seen one point at
a time.

Pulling back to `Spec 𝒪^{sh}_{X, p}` and reading the strict normal crossings condition at the
closed point expresses the extension of the stalk ideal `D_p` to `𝒪^{sh}_{X, p}` as the ideal
generated by the product of an initial segment of a regular system of parameters. Such a product
is a nonzerodivisor, and a principal ideal generated by a nonzerodivisor descends along a
henselization, so `D_p` is itself generated by a nonzerodivisor; regularity of `𝒪^{sh}_{X, p}`
descends to `𝒪_{X, p}`. By the stalkwise criterion of Tag 0AG8, `D` is therefore an effective
Cartier divisor, and `X` is regular at every point of `D`.

What is *not* available this way is the factorization of the local equation itself: the individual
branches of `D` exist over an étale neighbourhood of `p`, not over `𝒪_{X, p}`, which is exactly
why Tag 0CBS needs `X` to be J-2 or Nagata for the remaining content of (2) ⇒ (1).

## Main definitions

* `Stacks.Divisors.IsStrictNormalCrossingsAtStrictHenselizations` is condition (2) of Tag 0CBS.

## Main results

* `Stacks.Divisors.exists_isSystemOfParameters_map_stalk_of_comap_fromSpecStalk`: the extension of
  the stalk ideal to a strict henselization is generated by the product of an initial segment of a
  regular system of parameters.
* `Stacks.Divisors.isRegularLocalRing_stalk_of_isStrictNormalCrossingsAtStrictHenselizations`: the
  local ring at a point of `D` is regular.
* `exists_mem_nonZeroDivisors_stalk_eq_of_isStrictNormalCrossingsAtStrictHenselizations`: the
  stalk ideal at a point of `D` is generated by a nonzerodivisor.
* `Stacks.Divisors.isEffectiveCartierDivisor_of_isStrictNormalCrossingsAtStrictHenselizations`:
  `D` is an effective Cartier divisor.

## Implementation notes

The morphism `Spec 𝒪^{sh}_{X, p} ⟶ X` is `Spec.map φ ≫ X.fromSpecStalk p` for `φ` the structure
map of the strict henselization, matching the shape in which the forward implication of Tag 0CBS
is stated. Its closed point maps to `p`, and the induced map on stalks is `φ` once the stalk of
`Spec R` at the closed point is identified with `R` by
`AlgebraicGeometry.stalkClosedPointIso`; that is the content of the first private lemma, proved by
comparing germs on an affine open neighbourhood of `p` rather than by transporting along the
equality of points, which would require `eqToHom`.

Membership of the closed point in the support of the inverse image is obtained from the unit ideal
criterion: were the stalk of the inverse image the unit ideal, so would be the extension of `D_p`,
which consists of nonunits because `p` lies in the support of `D` and the structure map is local.

The strict normal crossings data lives in the stalk of `Spec R` at its closed point, so it is
transported to `R` along `stalkClosedPointIso`; a system of parameters generating the maximal
ideal transports along any ring equivalence of local rings, which is the second private lemma.
The existence of a strict henselization in the universe of the stalk is Stacks 04GP, packaged as
`IsLocalRing.exists_isHenselization_separableClosure`, and descent of regularity is Stacks 06LN.

## References

* [Stacks Project, Tag 0CBS](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/0CBS)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 0AG8](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/0AG8)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 04GP](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/04GP)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 06LN](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/06LN)
-/

@[expose] public noncomputable section

open AlgebraicGeometry CategoryTheory IsLocalRing

universe u

namespace Stacks.Divisors

/-- The stalk ideal of the inverse image of `D` under `Spec.map φ ≫ X.fromSpecStalk x`, read at
the closed point of `Spec R` and transported to `R`, is the extension of the stalk ideal of `D` at
`x` along `φ`. -/
private theorem map_stalk_comap_fromSpecStalk_closedPoint {X : Scheme.{u}}
    (D : X.IdealSheafData) (x : X) {R : CommRingCat.{u}} [IsLocalRing R]
    (φ : X.presheaf.stalk x ⟶ R) [IsLocalHom φ.hom] :
    (AlgebraicGeometry.IdealSheafData.stalk
        (D.comap (Spec.map φ ≫ X.fromSpecStalk x)) (closedPoint R)).map
          (AlgebraicGeometry.stalkClosedPointIso R).hom.hom
      = (AlgebraicGeometry.IdealSheafData.stalk D x).map φ.hom := by
  obtain ⟨U, hxU⟩ := exists_affineOpens_mem x
  have hgc : (Spec.map φ ≫ X.fromSpecStalk x) (closedPoint R) = x :=
    (congrArg (X.fromSpecStalk x).base.hom
      (AlgebraicGeometry.Spec_closedPoint (f := φ))).trans
      AlgebraicGeometry.Scheme.fromSpecStalk_closedPoint
  have hgU : (Spec.map φ ≫ X.fromSpecStalk x) (closedPoint R) ∈ U.1 := by rw [hgc]; exact hxU
  rw [AlgebraicGeometry.stalk_comap D (Spec.map φ ≫ X.fromSpecStalk x) (closedPoint R),
    AlgebraicGeometry.IdealSheafData.stalk_eq_map_germ D _ U hgU,
    AlgebraicGeometry.IdealSheafData.stalk_eq_map_germ D x U hxU,
    Ideal.map_map, Ideal.map_map, Ideal.map_map]
  congr 1
  have hgerm := AlgebraicGeometry.Scheme.germ_stalkClosedPointTo_Spec_fromSpecStalk
    (X := X) (R := R) φ U.1 hgU
  rw [AlgebraicGeometry.Scheme.stalkClosedPointTo] at hgerm
  have hgerm' := congrArg CommRingCat.Hom.hom hgerm
  simp only [CommRingCat.hom_comp] at hgerm'
  exact hgerm'

/-- A system of parameters generating the maximal ideal transports along a ring equivalence of
local rings. -/
private theorem isSystemOfParameters_map_of_ringEquiv {A B : Type u} [CommRing A] [IsLocalRing A]
    [CommRing B] [IsLocalRing B] (e : A ≃+* B) {rs : List A}
    (hgen : Ideal.ofList rs = maximalIdeal A) (hsop : IsSystemOfParameters rs) :
    IsSystemOfParameters (rs.map e.toRingHom) ∧
      Ideal.ofList (rs.map e.toRingHom) = maximalIdeal B := by
  have hmap : Ideal.ofList (rs.map e.toRingHom) = maximalIdeal B := by
    rw [← Ideal.map_ofList e.toRingHom rs, hgen]
    exact IsLocalRing.map_maximalIdeal_of_surjective e.toRingHom e.surjective
  refine ⟨⟨?_, ?_⟩, hmap⟩
  · rw [hmap]
    exact (maximalIdeal.isMaximal B).isPrime.radical
  · rw [← ringKrullDim_eq_of_ringEquiv e, hsop.2, List.length_map]

/-- **Condition (2) of Stacks Project, Tag 0CBS.** A closed subscheme of a locally Noetherian
scheme whose inverse image under the canonical morphism from the spectrum of a strict
henselization of the local ring at any of its points is a strict normal crossings divisor. -/
public abbrev IsStrictNormalCrossingsAtStrictHenselizations {X : Scheme.{u}}
    [IsLocallyNoetherian X] (D : X.IdealSheafData) : Prop :=
  ∀ x : X, (∃ y : D.subscheme, D.subschemeι y = x) →
    ∀ (L : Type u) [Field L] [Algebra (ResidueField (X.presheaf.stalk x)) L]
      [IsSepClosure (ResidueField (X.presheaf.stalk x)) L]
      (Ash : Type u) [CommRing Ash] [IsLocalRing Ash] [Algebra (X.presheaf.stalk x) Ash]
      [IsHenselization (X.presheaf.stalk x) L Ash],
      haveI : IsNoetherianRing Ash :=
        IsLocalRing.isNoetherianRing_of_isHenselization (A := X.presheaf.stalk x) L
      IsStrictNormalCrossingsDivisor (D.comap
        (Spec.map (CommRingCat.ofHom (algebraMap (X.presheaf.stalk x) Ash)) ≫
          X.fromSpecStalk x))

/-- **The local equation in a local algebra over the stalk.** Let `x` be a point of the support of
`D` and let `R` be a Noetherian local algebra over `𝒪_{X, x}` with local structure map, such that
the inverse image of `D` under the induced morphism `Spec R ⟶ X` is a strict normal crossings
divisor. Then `R` is a regular local ring and the extension of the stalk ideal of `D` at `x` to
`R` is generated by the product of a nonempty initial segment of a regular system of parameters of
`R`. -/
theorem exists_isSystemOfParameters_map_stalk_of_comap_fromSpecStalk {X : Scheme.{u}}
    (D : X.IdealSheafData) (x : X) (hx : x ∈ D.support)
    {R : Type u} [CommRing R] [IsLocalRing R] [IsNoetherianRing R]
    [Algebra (X.presheaf.stalk x) R] [IsLocalHom (algebraMap (X.presheaf.stalk x) R)]
    (hSNC : IsStrictNormalCrossingsDivisor (D.comap (Spec.map (CommRingCat.ofHom
      (algebraMap (X.presheaf.stalk x) R)) ≫ X.fromSpecStalk x))) :
    IsRegularLocalRing R ∧ ∃ (hs : List R) (s : ℕ), IsSystemOfParameters hs ∧
      Ideal.ofList hs = maximalIdeal R ∧ 1 ≤ s ∧ s ≤ hs.length ∧
      (AlgebraicGeometry.IdealSheafData.stalk D x).map (algebraMap (X.presheaf.stalk x) R)
        = Ideal.span {(hs.take s).prod} := by
  set φ : X.presheaf.stalk x ⟶ CommRingCat.of R :=
    CommRingCat.ofHom (algebraMap (X.presheaf.stalk x) R) with hφ
  have hφhom : φ.hom = algebraMap (X.presheaf.stalk x) R := rfl
  have : IsLocalHom φ.hom := hφhom ▸ inferInstance
  set e : ((Spec (CommRingCat.of R)).presheaf.stalk (closedPoint ↑(CommRingCat.of R)) : Type u)
      ≃+* R :=
    (AlgebraicGeometry.stalkClosedPointIso (CommRingCat.of R)).commRingCatIsoToRingEquiv with he
  have hkey := map_stalk_comap_fromSpecStalk_closedPoint D x φ
  -- The extension of the stalk ideal consists of nonunits, as the structure map is local.
  have hle : (AlgebraicGeometry.IdealSheafData.stalk D x).map φ.hom ≤ maximalIdeal R := by
    refine le_trans (Ideal.map_mono ?_) (IsLocalRing.map_maximalIdeal_le φ.hom)
    exact (stalk_le_maximalIdeal_iff_mem_support D x).mpr hx
  have hsupp : closedPoint ↑(CommRingCat.of R) ∈
      (D.comap (Spec.map φ ≫ X.fromSpecStalk x)).support := by
    by_contra hns
    rw [(stalk_eq_top_iff_notMem_support (D.comap (Spec.map φ ≫ X.fromSpecStalk x))
      (closedPoint ↑(CommRingCat.of R))).mpr hns, Ideal.map_top] at hkey
    exact (maximalIdeal.isMaximal R).ne_top (top_le_iff.mp (hkey ▸ hle))
  obtain ⟨hreg, rs, r, hrs, hgen, hr1, hrle, hstalk⟩ :=
    exists_isSystemOfParameters_stalk_eq_of_isStrictNormalCrossingsDivisor
      (D.comap (Spec.map φ ≫ X.fromSpecStalk x)) hSNC _ hsupp
  obtain ⟨hsop', hgen'⟩ := isSystemOfParameters_map_of_ringEquiv e hgen hrs
  have hR : IsRegularLocalRing R := IsRegularLocalRing.of_ringEquiv e
  have hcoe : e.toRingHom =
      (AlgebraicGeometry.stalkClosedPointIso (CommRingCat.of R)).hom.hom :=
    rfl
  have hfinal : (AlgebraicGeometry.IdealSheafData.stalk D x).map
      (algebraMap (X.presheaf.stalk x) R)
      = Ideal.span {((rs.map e.toRingHom).take r).prod} := by
    have hprod : ((rs.map e.toRingHom).take r).prod = e.toRingHom ((rs.take r).prod) := by
      rw [← List.map_take]
      exact (map_list_prod e.toRingHom (rs.take r)).symm
    rw [hprod, hcoe, ← hφhom, ← hkey, hstalk, Ideal.map_span, Set.image_singleton]
  exact ⟨hR, rs.map e.toRingHom, r, hsop', hgen', hr1,
    by rw [List.length_map]; exact hrle, hfinal⟩

/-- The local ring is regular and the stalk ideal is generated by a nonzerodivisor, at a point of
the support of a closed subscheme with strict normal crossings at the strict henselizations. -/
private theorem isRegularLocalRing_and_exists_stalk_eq_span {X : Scheme.{u}}
    [IsLocallyNoetherian X] (D : X.IdealSheafData)
    (hD : IsStrictNormalCrossingsAtStrictHenselizations D) (x : X) (hx : x ∈ D.support) :
    IsRegularLocalRing (X.presheaf.stalk x) ∧
      ∃ f ∈ nonZeroDivisors (X.presheaf.stalk x),
        AlgebraicGeometry.IdealSheafData.stalk D x = Ideal.span {f} := by
  obtain ⟨y, hy⟩ : ∃ y : D.subscheme, D.subschemeι y = x :=
    (Scheme.IdealSheafData.range_subschemeι (I := D)).ge hx
  set A := (X.presheaf.stalk x : Type u) with hA
  set L := SeparableClosure (ResidueField A) with hL
  obtain ⟨Ash, _, _, _, _⟩ := IsLocalRing.exists_isHenselization_separableClosure A
  have : IsNoetherianRing Ash := IsLocalRing.isNoetherianRing_of_isHenselization (A := A) L
  have : IsLocalHom (algebraMap A Ash) := IsLocalRing.IsHenselization.isLocalHom (L := L)
  obtain ⟨hreg, hs, s, hsop, hsgen, -, -, hmap⟩ :=
    exists_isSystemOfParameters_map_stalk_of_comap_fromSpecStalk D x hx (hD x ⟨y, hy⟩ L Ash)
  have := hreg
  have hnzd : (hs.take s).prod ∈ nonZeroDivisors Ash :=
    IsRegularLocalRing.mem_nonZeroDivisors_prod_take_of_ofList_eq_maximalIdeal hsop hsgen s
  obtain ⟨Ah, _, _, _, _⟩ := IsLocalRing.exists_isHenselization_residueField A
  refine ⟨((isRegularLocalRing_iff_henselizations A Ah Ash L).2).mpr hreg, ?_⟩
  exact exists_mem_nonZeroDivisors_span_singleton_eq_of_isHenselization L _ hnzd hmap

/-- **The ambient scheme is regular along the divisor.** At a point of the support of a closed
subscheme with strict normal crossings at the strict henselizations, the local ring of the ambient
scheme is regular. -/
theorem isRegularLocalRing_stalk_of_isStrictNormalCrossingsAtStrictHenselizations
    {X : Scheme.{u}} [IsLocallyNoetherian X] (D : X.IdealSheafData)
    (hD : IsStrictNormalCrossingsAtStrictHenselizations D) (x : X) (hx : x ∈ D.support) :
    IsRegularLocalRing (X.presheaf.stalk x) :=
  (isRegularLocalRing_and_exists_stalk_eq_span D hD x hx).1

/-- **The local equation descends from the strict henselization.** At a point of the support of a
closed subscheme with strict normal crossings at the strict henselizations, the stalk ideal is
generated by a single nonzerodivisor. -/
theorem exists_mem_nonZeroDivisors_stalk_eq_of_isStrictNormalCrossingsAtStrictHenselizations
    {X : Scheme.{u}} [IsLocallyNoetherian X] (D : X.IdealSheafData)
    (hD : IsStrictNormalCrossingsAtStrictHenselizations D) (x : X) (hx : x ∈ D.support) :
    ∃ f ∈ nonZeroDivisors (X.presheaf.stalk x),
      AlgebraicGeometry.IdealSheafData.stalk D x = Ideal.span {f} :=
  (isRegularLocalRing_and_exists_stalk_eq_span D hD x hx).2

/-- **Stacks Project, Tag 0CBS, the effective Cartier divisor conjunct of (2) ⇒ (1).** A closed
subscheme of a locally Noetherian scheme whose inverse image to the spectrum of a strict
henselization of the local ring at each of its points is a strict normal crossings divisor is an
effective Cartier divisor. No J-2 or Nagata hypothesis is needed for this conjunct: the local
equation is recovered one point at a time by descent along the henselization. -/
@[stacks 0CBS "(2) ⇒ (1), the effective Cartier divisor conjunct of condition (1). The
étale-local strict normal crossings clause of (1) is not asserted, and no J-2 or Nagata
hypothesis is used for this conjunct."]
theorem isEffectiveCartierDivisor_of_isStrictNormalCrossingsAtStrictHenselizations
    {X : Scheme.{u}} [IsLocallyNoetherian X] (D : X.IdealSheafData)
    (hD : IsStrictNormalCrossingsAtStrictHenselizations D) :
    IsEffectiveCartierDivisor D :=
  isEffectiveCartierDivisor_of_stalk_isPrincipal_nonZeroDivisor D fun x hx ↦
    exists_mem_nonZeroDivisors_stalk_eq_of_isStrictNormalCrossingsAtStrictHenselizations D hD x hx

end Stacks.Divisors

end
